{% load public_url_tags %}
{% comment %}
Persistent trust-center nav, rendered under the brand header on every public
page.

A reader who lands on an advisory or a component page from a search result or a
customer email has no other way back to the workspace root — the logo is a link,
but nothing says so. This makes "where am I and how do I get back" answerable
from any page.

Renders nothing when no workspace can be resolved, which is how the public pages
that are not part of a trust center (standalone document and VDP pages) opt out
without needing to know about this file.
{% endcomment %}
{% workspace_public_url as tc_home_url %}
{% workspace_advisories_url as tc_advisories_url %}
{% if tc_home_url %}
    {% comment %}
        The sticky band and the width-limited track are layout, which a page
        owns; the row of destinations and the current marker are the component's.

        The band draws the rule so it spans the viewport rather than stopping
        at the track, which is why the nav is flush. px-4 matches the page
        header's track, so the first destination lines up with the title.

        The track scrolls on a narrow screen, with the scrollbar hidden: it
        would otherwise sit under the destinations on every page, and there is
        nothing below the nav to scroll it away.
    {% endcomment %}
    <div class="sticky top-0 z-[60] border-b border-solid border-border bg-[color-mix(in_oklab,var(--color-background)_92%,transparent)] backdrop-blur-[10px]">
        <div class="mx-auto max-w-[1200px] px-4 overflow-x-auto [scrollbar-width:none] [&::-webkit-scrollbar]:hidden">
            <c-branded.nav flush aria-label="Trust center">
            {% comment %}
                The current flag is written as two whole tags rather than
                :current="request.path == tc_home_url". Cotton's colon prefix
                resolves a variable, not an expression, so a comparison there
                evaluates falsy in silence and the nav simply never marks a
                current page.
            {% endcomment %}
            {% if request.path == tc_home_url %}
                <c-branded.nav-item href="{{ tc_home_url }}" icon="fas fa-house" current>Overview</c-branded.nav-item>
            {% else %}
                <c-branded.nav-item href="{{ tc_home_url }}" icon="fas fa-house">Overview</c-branded.nav-item>
            {% endif %}
            {% if tc_advisories_url %}
                {# startswith, so an advisory detail page still marks the section current. #}
                {% if tc_advisories_url in request.path %}
                    <c-branded.nav-item href="{{ tc_advisories_url }}" icon="fas fa-shield-halved" current>Security advisories</c-branded.nav-item>
                {% else %}
                    <c-branded.nav-item href="{{ tc_advisories_url }}" icon="fas fa-shield-halved">Security advisories</c-branded.nav-item>
                {% endif %}
            {% endif %}
            </c-branded.nav>
        </div>
    </div>
{% endif %}
